---
import { Image } from "astro:assets"
import Feature from "../../layouts/Feature.astro"
import Beat from "../../components/Beat.astro"
import Term from "../../components/Term.astro"
import terminals from "../../assets/console/terminals.png"

const faq = [
  {
    q: "How is this different from tmux over SSH?",
    a: "tmux keeps a shell alive, but you still need a way in: an open port, keys, and a reconnect by hand after every drop. Paperboat keeps the shell alive, reconnects on its own and needs no open port. You can still run tmux inside it.",
  },
  {
    q: "How is this different from mosh?",
    a: "mosh handles roaming, but needs UDP ports open on the server. Paperboat needs nothing opened, shows the output you missed when you return, and the same shell can be opened from a second device or shared.",
  },
  {
    q: "How much output is shown when I come back?",
    a: "The most recent output, up to 64 KiB, then it's live again. For long logs, write to a file or run tmux inside the session.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which shell does it run?",
    a: "Your own login shell on that machine: bash, zsh, fish or PowerShell, with your normal dotfiles. Full-screen programs such as vim, htop and less work, with colours and resizing.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many terminals can I open?",
    a: "From the pb command, as many as you like, on every plan. In the web console, 10 at once on Free and 100 on Pro.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can Paperboat read my terminal?",
    a: 'No. Terminal traffic is encrypted between your two machines, and from your browser when you use the console. See <a href="/security/">security</a>.',
  },
]
---

<Feature
  slug="terminal"
  title="Terminals that keep running | Paperboat"
  description="Terminals that keep running when your laptop sleeps or the network drops, and show you what you missed."
  headline="Terminals that keep running"
  faq={faq}
  related={["recordings", "ssh", "console"]}
  compare={["ssh-bastion", "tailscale", "vscode-tunnels"]}
>
  <p slot="lede">Open a shell on any of your machines. Close the laptop, switch networks, come back tomorrow: it's still running.</p>
  <Term
    slot="aside"
    lines={[
      "$ pb connect studio",
      "ana@studio:~$ ./train.sh",
      "epoch 1/40   loss 2.31",
      "# close the laptop, go home",
      "$ pb connect studio",
      "epoch 31/40  loss 0.42",
    ]}
  />

  <Beat id="back-title" title="Pick up where you left off" wide>
    <p>The shell runs on the machine, not on your laptop. When you come back, you see what you missed, and you're live again.</p>
    <figure slot="visual" class="shot">
      <Image src={terminals} alt="The console's Terminals page: four open terminals on studio, gpu-box and staging, one in use." widths={[1136, 2272]} sizes="1136px" format="png" />
    </figure>
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="anywhere-title" title="From any computer, or a browser">
    <p>Open the same shell from your laptop, your desktop or a browser tab. Type in one and it shows in all of them.</p>
    <Term
      slot="visual"
      lines={["$ pb session list studio", "NAME      PROCESS    STATE", "default   train.sh   running", "logs      tail       running", "$ pb connect studio --session logs"]}
    />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="share-title" title="Work in one shell together" flip>
    <p>Let a teammate watch a live shell, or type in it with you. Remove them and they're out at once.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb session share S12 --team acme --all", "# everyone on acme can watch", "$ pb session unshare S12"]} />
  </Beat>

  <section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="details-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="details-title">Details</h2>
      <div class="points points-3">
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Your own shell</h3>
          <p>bash, zsh, fish or PowerShell, with your dotfiles. vim, htop and less just work.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Several per machine</h3>
          <p>Name your sessions, keep a build in one and logs in another, switch any time.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Record when it matters</h3>
          <p><a href="/features/recordings/">Record a session</a> and play it back later, step by step.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Feature>

<style>
  .shot {
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--paper);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px rgb(20 20 20 / 0.08),
      0 24px 48px -32px rgb(20 20 20 / 0.18);
  }

  .shot :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
